  "body": "## What changed\n\n`verify` passes the path through one door before any law runs (`crates/sim/src/verify/axis_door.rs`, new; wired in `verify/engine.rs`):\n\n- An axis with a **non-finite** component, **zero length**, or a length that **overflows** is refused by name with `Warning::NonFinite { at }`. The NonFinite law now covers `axis` as well as `from`/`to`; its text now reads \"non-finite coordinate or tool axis\". The refused axis is kept as stated, so each law's own guard still fires. For example, the radial rapid law's conviction of a zero pose stands.\n- A **finite, non-unit** axis (`|a|²` more than 1e-12 off 1) is **normalised once** in a copy that every law reads.\n- Already-unit axes pass bit for bit through a borrowed `Cow`: no copy, and no existing verdict or golden moves.\n\nDecision record: `docs/decisions/1312-verify-axis-refusal.md`. The reachability search the issue asks for is on the issue: no generator, CL import or MCP path emits such an axis, so the issue stays P3.\n\n## How tested\n\n- Pinning tests in `crates/sim/tests/axis_door.rs` (new, 5 tests). Four of them fail on main and pass here:\n  - `a_non_finite_axis_is_refused_by_name`: reproduction 1, `[1e-12, 0, inf]` and others.\n  - `a_scaled_axis_is_judged_as_its_unit_direction`: reproduction 2, the 7x axis at 2e-9 rad keeps its `ShankHit`.\n  - `a_zero_or_overflowing_axis_is_refused_by_name`\n  - `one_bad_axis_refuses_only_its_own_move`\n- Unit tests in `verify::axis_door::tests` (2).\n- `radial_rapids::a_rapid_on_a_pose_that_is_no_direction_convicts_itself`: its exact assertion now also expects the added `NonFinite { at: 0 }`. The `RapidInStock` conviction is unchanged.\n- Quick-gate plan (`cargo xtask gate quick --base upstream/main`): every sim suite whose gate map names `sim::verify` plus the sim lib, 272 tests, all green on the final head. Motion `real_tip` and `solid_law` green. The 47 mapped app suites ran green (533 s) on the first variant of the door, which dropped a refused axis to upright. That gate run was VOID only because I edited files during it. The final variant differs only for refused axes, which no app suite feeds verify (grep-checked).\n- `cargo clippy -p camcraft-sim --all-targets -- -D warnings`: clean.\n\n## Not exercised\n\n- The mapped app suites were not re-run on the final head. See above for why.\n- The other public law entries the post gate calls directly (`bands_vs_fixtures`, `rapids_vs_fixtures_spindle`) do not go through the door. The search found no path that feeds them a bad axis.\n- Release-lane heavy tests were not run.\n\nChangelog: Verify refuses a move whose tool axis is non-finite or of zero length, and judges a non-unit axis by its unit direction (#1312)\n\nEffort: high (no escalation)\n\nFork synced at upstream/main 53a52f88 (branch cut from upstream/main).\n\nFixes #1312\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n",
